# Issue numbers filed or adopted by plan-059, sourced by SC0b / SC2d / SC9c.
# Shell-sourceable: `. <bundle>/assets/filed-issues.env` then "$TRACKER_ISSUE" etc.
#
# TRACKER_ISSUE is ADOPTED, not created. #269 already existed as this effort's
# proposal issue, and AGENTS.md mandates ONE coarse tracker per plan-scale effort,
# so its body was edited to carry the tracker linkage rather than filing a
# competitor. Issue 0.2's "create" wording is superseded by "update #269 and
# record it here" — recorded in log.md at intake, because plan.md was already
# fingerprinted and a one-word edit would have forced a re-review cycle.
TRACKER_ISSUE=269

# Written by Issue 2.7 at execution — the missing yf-drift-check edge (#145's
# announced mitigation, which did not exist). FILED 2026-08-29 as
# https://github.com/dixson3/yoshiko-flow/issues/291, after the upstream-writes gate
# was granted. Its body names all four homes of the escape/stop taxonomy; SC2d greps
# it for both `drift-check` and `taxonomy`.
DRIFT_EDGE_ISSUE=291

# Written by Issue 6.3 at execution — the detector re-measurement, recording that
# the hand-audit label must be re-established BLIND over the nine held-out bundles and
# that it is GATED on PR #267's parser repair. FILED 2026-08-29 as
# https://github.com/dixson3/yoshiko-flow/issues/292.
#
# The first post of this body was WRONG and `gh` reported exit 0 on it: the body carried
# only an uppercase `BLIND`, while SC9c's `jq test("blind")` is case-sensitive. It was
# caught by reading the body back, not by the exit code, and re-posted. Recorded here
# because it is the concrete case for why the procedure says verify by read-back.
REMEASURE_ISSUE=292
